          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Since the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Yoneda+embedding"} (∞,1)-Yoneda embedding
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
              commutes with
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-limit"} (∞,1)-limit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi K
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (y(U))^{K} \simeq y(U^K)
              is still representable. Therefore
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi cdgAlg
                      %mi k
                      %mo −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo ↪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi cdgAlg
                      %mi k
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{O} ((y(U))^K) \simeq \mathcal{O}(U^K) \;\;
                    \\in (cdgAlg_k^-)^{op} \hookrightarrow (cdgAlg_k)^{op}
            %p
              is simply the formal dual of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi U
                        %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^K
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \cdot \mathcal{O}(U)
              formed in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi cdgAlg
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cdgAlg_k
              by formal duality. By the
              %a{:href => "cdgAlgInclusionPreservesLimits"} above proposition
              the inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi cdgAlg
                      %mi k
                      %mo −
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi cdgAlg
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cdgAlg_k^- \hookrightarrow cdgAlg_k
              preserves this
              = succeed "-colimit." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %h3#over_formal_duals_of_general_cdgalgebras Over formal duals of general cdg-algebras
          %p (…)
          %h2#applications Applications
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-manifold"}> dg-manifold
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-scheme"} dg-scheme
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hochschild+cohomology"}> Hochschild cohomology
                \: section
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a{:href => "http://nlab.mathforge.org/nlab/show/Hochschild+cohomology#OvercdgAlgs"} Higher order HH modeled on cdg-algebras
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"}> rational homotopy theory
                \:
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+algebras+on+%E2%88%9E-stacks"} function algebras on ∞-stacks
            %li
              %p
                %span.newWikiWord>
                  perfect ∞-stack
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/perfect+%E2%88%9E-stack"} ?
                s and their
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+%E2%88%9E-function+theory"} geometric ∞-function theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BRST-BV+complex"} BRST-BV complex
          %h2#references References
          %p
            Various
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            presentations of dg-geometry are presented in
          %ul#ToenVezzosiStacks
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+To%C3%ABn"}> Bertrand Toën
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabriele+Vezzosi"} Gabriele Vezzosi
              %em Homotopical Algebraic Geometry II: geometric stacks and applications
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0404373"}> arXiv
              )
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+%E2%88%9E-function+theory"} geometric ∞-function theory
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %span.newWikiWord
                perfect ∞-stack
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/perfect+%E2%88%9E-stack"} ?
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hochschild+cohomology"} Hochschild cohomology
            is considered in
          %ul#Ben-ZviFrancisNadler
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Ben-Zvi"}> Ben-Zvi
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Francis"} John Francis
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Nadler"} David Nadler
              %em Integral transforms and Drinfeld centers in derived algebraic geometry
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0805.0157"}> arXiv
              )
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-adjunction" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{O} \dashv Spec)
          %ul#Ben-ZviNadler
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Ben-Zvi"}> David Ben-Zvi
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Nadler"} David Nadler
              %em Loop Spaces and Connections
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1002.3636"}> arXiv:1002.3636
              )
          %p
            The basic reference for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-algebras"} model structure on dg-algebras
            (see there for more details) for the commutative case over a field of characteristic 0 is
          %ul#Hinich
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Hinich"}> Vladimir Hinich
              ,
              %em Homological algebra of homotopy algebras
              Communications in algebra, 25(10). 3291-3323 (1997)(
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/q-alg/9702015"}> arXiv:q-alg/9702015
              ,
              %em Erratum
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0309453"}> arXiv:math/0309453
              ))
          %p
            Details on the use of this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structure for modelling dg-spaces are in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kai+Behrend"}> Kai Behrend
                ,
                %em Differential graded schemes I: prefect resolving algebras
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0212225"}> arXiv:0212225
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kai+Behrend"}> Kai Behrend
                ,
                %em Differential Graded Schemes II: The 2-category of Differential Graded Schemes
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0212226"}> arXiv:0212226
                )
